   "stem": {
      "text": "The integral test is applied to the series \\( \\sum_{n=2}^{\\infty} \\frac{\\ln n}{n^{2}} \\). Take f(x) to be the series' general term with n replaced by x, and the lower limit of integration to be the series' starting index. Find the exact value of the improper integral of f from that lower limit to infinity."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Add",
         [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Ln",
               2
            ],
            2
         ],
